From f3bfdf8b8c08870754cc3c756b75faa9156595e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:34:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep expert swizzle opt-in and cover native widths

Retain the prior unswizzled default until hardware comparisons qualify a
panel. The ordering audit gives a counterexample to choosing panel 3
universally: expert pairs can straddle its boundaries. Correct the cache
and empty-tile documentation and verify default/explicit generated code.
Extend GPU equality cases to native TP3/TP4 widths with eight experts to
bound test memory; the compiler matrix separately covers all 384 experts.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Prepared-base: 1f33102547e4da5c64712390604695d1abd577c4
Parent: 5cc36f7662f77330efe7d40c141e1d79d38e2c37
Quality: preserve the actual old default; positive panels remain opt-in.
Tests: 72 CPU lowering cases, 949524 compiler-header grid coordinates,
48 workspace cases, four default-source comparisons against the base.
GPU equality, batch invariance and serving performance remain pending.
Upstream-status: draft review; no performance or promotion claim.
---
